WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.146 --> 00:00:09.146
(upbeat rock music)

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.090
- Hey guys, I'm Scott,
I'm a Tasty producer

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:17.500
and I've been challenged by Brenda

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.090
to make a 100-layer crepe cake.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:21.910
Last season, we had a producer

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.750
made a 100-layer lasagna
and when you hear that,

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.170
you would guess there's
100 lasagna noodles,

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:29.580
but he counted, like,
the sauce, bechemel...

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.200
When I'm gonna make 100-layer crepe cake,

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.400
there's going to be one-hund-red crepes.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.440
Let's get started.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:37.300
We made a lot of crepes on Tasty.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.630
This rainbow one is amazing, wow.

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:42.350
- [Brenda] Oh, imagine
doing 100 different colors.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.430
- I'm not doing that. (both laugh)

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:45.840
- [Brenda] What's that filling?

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:46.760
- I think its just whipped cream.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:47.740
We've got our recipe,
let's get our ingredients.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:48.657
Go, go, go!

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:50.830
It's like I'm on Top Chef or something.

00:00:50.830 --> 00:00:52.413
Flour, sugar, salt!

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:53.640
- [Brenda] You got 10 seconds.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.573
- I, that's all there is!

00:00:56.351 --> 00:00:57.184
- [Brenda Alright.
- Alright.

00:00:57.184 --> 00:00:59.600
Two tablespoons of butter,
the milk, and eggs,

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:01.783
we'll whisk that together, also--

00:01:01.783 --> 00:01:04.090
(glass shatters)

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:05.070
Ah!
- [Brenda] Aw,

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:06.410
it looks like a sad omelet.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:07.903
- Crepe one, pretty bad.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.457
Not, oh--
- [Brenda] Whoo, you got it!

00:01:10.457 --> 00:01:13.963
- Oh, nice!

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.723
We've made four and
it's been half an hour.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:19.710
I wanna get one of my favorite crepe cakes

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:21.810
in the city and sort of dissect it,

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:23.780
make sure that my crepe
tastes like their crepe.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:25.950
Alright, this is the best
crepe cake in New York

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:27.710
and there was a sign in there that said

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:30.550
there were 20 paper thin layers of crepe.

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:32.050
They're not counting
the filling as a layer,

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:34.030
so it seems like we're on the right track

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:35.339
counting 100 crepes..

00:01:35.339 --> 00:01:36.172
- It's mostly filling.

00:01:36.172 --> 00:01:38.020
- Yeah, it's like a sweetened whip cream

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:41.160
and just a so delicate
and thin of a crepe.

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.370
I think this was good research.

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:43.740
- [Brenda] Yes.
- I think I need

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.380
to make my crepes thinner
- [Brenda] Okay.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:46.400
- I think...

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:49.970
That's all I really learned. (both laugh)

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:50.940
We're back, day two.

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:53.363
I feel like I'm pretty
good going into today.

00:01:53.410 --> 00:01:54.550
Yesterday we used three eggs,

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:56.410
today we're gonna use 24 eggs.

00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:58.340
One of our Tasty writers made a post,

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:01.020
how to make a perfect crepe
according to a French person,

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.760
so now we're gonna take her recipe,

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.770
scale that up to a hundred
and make a crepe cake.

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.470
This is the biggest bowl we
have in the Tasty kitchen.

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:08.927
I don't know how I'm
gonna get this in there.

00:02:08.927 --> 00:02:11.760
(egg cracks)
(playful flute music)

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.500
Wow, so many eggs.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.129
I could use about seven more
people to help with this.

00:02:18.129 --> 00:02:21.200
(playful flute music)

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.393
Add the cooled butter.

00:02:22.499 --> 00:02:24.582
- [Brenda] Ooh...
- What?

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:26.640
I feel good about this.

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:30.895
My hand is like, I can't actually

00:02:30.895 --> 00:02:32.150
straighten my hand anymore.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:34.040
This looks right, this
looks like as creamy

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:34.880
as it's supposed to look.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:36.040
We're gonna let this set for an hour.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:37.513
I think we're in a good place.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.250
Not perfect, ah, we're getting there!

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:42.420
We were so close, nice!

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:44.040
I need a paper and a pen and we need

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.883
to just start tallying these up.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:47.820
Yes, oh!
- [Brenda] No!

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:49.250
- It's still usable.

00:02:49.824 --> 00:02:50.763
(both gasp)

00:02:50.763 --> 00:02:52.052
What?
- [Brenda] How?

00:02:52.052 --> 00:02:53.343
- [Scott] That is a good crepe.

00:02:53.343 --> 00:02:55.420
- Whoa, hold on.
- [Scott] Go, go, go, go, go!

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:56.323
- This is scary.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:00.324
Oh my god, Scott, this is, I'm sorry.

00:03:00.324 --> 00:03:03.500
- 50 crepes!
(Brenda claps)

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:05.550
- [Brenda] That was the
saddest celebration.

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:07.230
- Let me know when we're at a hundred.

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:09.543
This is the 99th crepe.

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:11.600
Wow, my heart is racing.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.173
Number 100, comin' atcha.

00:03:14.162 --> 00:03:15.231
(crepe lands)
(applause)

00:03:15.231 --> 00:03:17.898
- [Woman] That's it!
- [All] Yay!

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:21.173
- Alright, it's day
three, we made 100 crepes.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:23.273
We've had a bit of an oversight here.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:25.190
So it's not supposed to
be just whipped cream,

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:27.080
it needs to be a pastry cream, that way,

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:29.030
when all this weight is on top of it,

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:30.713
it just doesn't squeeze out.

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:33.210
We have to make a huge
batch of pastry cream

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:35.603
and then we also wanna make four flavors.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:37.950
Do you have any advice
on, like, how to tackle

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:40.033
making these four flavors?

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:42.020
I'm thinking, based on how I know

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:44.840
to make pastry cream,
mix in butter and vanilla

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:46.730
when it's hot at the end, would you get

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:47.567
like a stockpot
- [Jesse] Yes.

00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:49.390
- [Scott] And just make pastry cream?

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:51.333
- Yes, just make one big pastry cream.

00:03:52.314 --> 00:03:54.850
(laid back drum beat)

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:57.430
And then, for strawberry,
I would get a jam

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:59.060
and then chocolate, just literally chop up

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:00.720
some chocolate and throw
it in when it's hot

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.870
and then it'll melt
and you can fold it in.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:05.440
Vanilla, I'd just add
paste, vanilla bean paste

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:07.870
or even extract and matcha,
when it's still hot,

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:10.900
I would put it in, like,
a fine sieve or a strainer

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:12.830
and then do this and then
fold it in and do this

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:14.530
and fold it and it should be fine.

00:04:14.615 --> 00:04:17.782
(laid back drum beat)

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:18.737
- [Scott] I think it's all gonna have

00:04:18.737 --> 00:04:21.370
we'll add vanilla extract
to the overall cream

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:22.920
and we'll kinda keep that...
- [Jesse] Just leave

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:23.753
that one plain then?
- [Scott] Leave

00:04:23.753 --> 00:04:24.586
that one plain.

00:04:25.322 --> 00:04:28.535
(goofy classical music)

00:04:28.535 --> 00:04:30.980
(tape tears loudly)

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:32.560
Oh my gosh!
- [Brenda] Is that a,

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:33.980
what the heck is this?

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:35.240
- Something Vaughn said yesterday

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:36.940
really stuck with me, he said I wasn't

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:38.680
being original or big enough.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:41.020
I'm not in the business
of not going all out.

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:43.010
If we assemble this crepe
cake, it's just gonna

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:46.260
be this Leaning Tower of Pisa situation.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:48.603
This is, like, cute, it's a crepe.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:51.880
This, tell me we shouldn't be doing this.

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:53.833
You know what I have to do.

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:55.393
Oh, it's tearing!

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:57.193
This will go to the crepe graveyard.

00:04:58.061 --> 00:04:59.593
No, this is terrible.

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:02.553
- [Brenda] Scott, that's awesome!

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:03.940
That looks really good!

00:05:04.701 --> 00:05:05.534
Oh!
- Wow!

00:05:06.771 --> 00:05:08.480
(peaceful marimba music)

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:10.350
I may have lost track of what day,

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:11.693
exactly, it is.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:13.860
We spent a lot of time
with the giant crepe maker.

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:15.440
I'm not gonna be satisfied if we go

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.130
with the smaller one and yesterday,

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:18.443
Brenda got me this guy.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:21.360
It makes them perfectly
thin, it uses less batter.

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:23.563
We've got 100 crepes to make, let's do it!

00:05:24.242 --> 00:05:27.659
(peaceful marimba music)

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:30.713
I am 900% crepe right now.

00:05:31.346 --> 00:05:33.246
(sighs) Oh my god, I lost count again.

00:05:33.373 --> 00:05:35.653
Nobody is here! (laughs)

00:05:35.653 --> 00:05:36.486
I think I'm losing it.

00:05:36.486 --> 00:05:38.540
I don't think this was designed to be on

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:41.870
for this amount of time,
so I'm overall impressed

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:43.153
that it's still working.

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:45.766
Sometimes, life gives you crepes.

00:05:45.766 --> 00:05:48.683
(cricket chirping)

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:49.740
You gotta make...

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:51.883
Good crepes and bad crepes.

00:05:51.883 --> 00:05:53.083
That's not a saying.

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:55.570
This is number...

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:57.023
Almost 90.

00:05:57.110 --> 00:05:59.530
This is taking a lot longer
than I thought it would,

00:05:59.530 --> 00:06:02.193
it's very late, nobody is here.

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:04.448
Here we go. (sighs)

00:06:04.448 --> 00:06:06.306
(pants and whispers) Yes!

00:06:06.306 --> 00:06:08.606
(normal voice) Here we
go, bringing in 90, ah!

00:06:09.666 --> 00:06:10.499
Oh, f--

00:06:10.506 --> 00:06:12.606
Okay, 90's not beautiful, but that's fine.

00:06:12.757 --> 00:06:14.273
This is our last crepe.

00:06:15.618 --> 00:06:18.147
(chuckles) I'm losin' it.

00:06:18.147 --> 00:06:20.355
(sizzling)

00:06:20.355 --> 00:06:21.188
(whispers) Hurry up, crepe.

00:06:21.188 --> 00:06:22.763
I think it's done, which means I'm done.

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:24.063
For today at least!

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:26.333
At least when I made the first 100 crepes,

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:30.065
there was like a room that
fake applauded for me.

00:06:30.065 --> 00:06:32.315
(applause)

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:34.440
Nobody's here to celebrate with me.

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:37.430
We did it, we got a giant crepe cake,

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:39.433
hundred layer coming soon.

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:41.993
Whoo!

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:46.400
This is it, I'm going to
work, this is our last day

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:48.250
of the hundred layer giant crepe cake.

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:51.023
I stayed after last night
to make all the fillings.

00:06:51.035 --> 00:06:52.340
This is it, this is the last day,

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:53.173
make or break.

00:06:53.665 --> 00:06:55.316
(cool drum beat)

00:06:55.316 --> 00:06:56.763
This is gonna be amazing.

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:01.970
Alright, this is 49, one more

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:03.173
and we're halfway there.

00:07:03.265 --> 00:07:04.860
- I'm about to start crying.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:05.945
- You're about to start crying?

00:07:05.945 --> 00:07:07.660
- This adventure's almost done.

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.110
- Still don't know if
the other pastry creams

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:10.513
have firmed up, hopefully.

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:14.390
- [Brenda] What layer is this?

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:17.273
- Honestly, Brenda, I don't know. (laughs)

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:18.683
This is 50.

00:07:18.683 --> 00:07:19.820
We are officially

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:22.483
- [Brenda] Whoo!
- Halfway done.

00:07:23.129 --> 00:07:26.546
(upbeat inspiring music)

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.313
This is number 99! (screams)

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:32.663
Number 100!

00:07:34.409 --> 00:07:36.409
[Scott And Brenda] Whoo!

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:38.770
Thank you, wow, I'm lightheaded!

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:40.140
We're gonna throw this guy in the freezer,

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:41.870
dust it with some powdered sugar later,

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:43.670
and then we'll cut it and we'll serve it

00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:45.813
and it's gonna be grand.

00:07:45.992 --> 00:07:49.075
(upbeat dance music)

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:51.300
- [Brenda] Okay, it's cutting pretty well!

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:54.943
- Oh, I feel every layer,
it's so satisfying!

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:59.867
- [Brenda] (gasps) Oh my god! (laughs)

00:08:01.272 --> 00:08:02.522
- I don't know!

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:07.743
What in the actual world?

00:08:08.981 --> 00:08:10.314
- That's insane!

00:08:11.531 --> 00:08:12.750
- [Scott] Can we get that in the freezer?

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:14.167
- Yeah, seriously, oh!

00:08:15.693 --> 00:08:18.193
(Scott gasps)

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:19.093
Scott, you're just gonna have

00:08:19.093 --> 00:08:20.140
to cut another one.

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:22.390
You're just gonna have
to, okay, I'm leaving.

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:25.960
I'm gonna leave this production right now,

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:28.113
so Scott's gonna be by himself.

00:08:28.899 --> 00:08:31.423
Oh no, Scott, I'm so sorry!

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:34.333
- Let's just try again.
- Yeah!

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:37.963
We still gotta eat it.

00:08:38.811 --> 00:08:41.394
(upbeat music)

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:51.560
- Steven's here to inspect if I actually

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:53.333
got 100 layers, which I did,

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:54.980
so I don't know why he's here.

00:08:55.363 --> 00:08:57.363
- One, two, three, four.

00:08:58.981 --> 00:09:01.981
(sped-up squeaking)

00:09:04.661 --> 00:09:09.661
99, 100!
(Scott and Brenda whoop)

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:14.053
- Scott just gave birth, he's a new mom.

00:09:14.413 --> 00:09:15.746
(Scott whistling)

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:17.270
- [Scott] Giant crepe cake coming through.

00:09:17.270 --> 00:09:18.893
It's so heavy.

00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:21.240
We've got four flavors,
chocolate, strawberry,

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:22.410
matcha and vanilla.

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:23.510
Does anyone want some?

00:09:23.831 --> 00:09:26.530
(everyone laughs)

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:29.640
We did it, we conquered
the 100-layer crepe cake

00:09:29.850 --> 00:09:32.580
and it was cool, to see how, when I sent

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:34.760
the message to the office,
people did come down.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:37.453
It is the biggest, craziest
thing I've ever made.

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:39.060
I think we made some people happy

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:40.813
and that's what really matters.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:45.253
This piece is much too large. (laughs)

00:09:46.178 --> 00:09:49.345
(laid back bass vibe)

00:09:57.221 --> 00:09:59.888
(camera clicks)

